  'x.best7': 'In Texas hold\'em you use the best five of seven cards: your two and the five on the board. You may use both, one or none of yours.',
  'tip.best7': 'Look for matching ranks first, then five of a suit, then five in a row.',
  'x.flow': 'If nobody has bet you may check or bet. If someone has, you fold, call (match) or raise. When every bet is matched the round ends.',
  'tip.flow': 'You cannot check once someone has bet.',
  'x.pos': 'Left of the dealer button (D) is the small blind, then the big blind. Preflop the player left of the big blind (UTG) acts first; after the flop play starts left of the button. The button acts last — the best seat.',
  'tip.pos': 'Acting last, you see what others do before you decide.',
  'x.outs': 'Outs are the unseen cards that make your hand. A flush draw (four of a suit) has 9, an open-ended straight draw 8, a gutshot 4.',
  'tip.outs': 'With a flush and a straight draw do not count shared cards twice.',
  'x.rule24': 'On the flop (two cards to come) outs × 4 ≈ your % to hit; on the turn (one card) outs × 2.',
  'tip.rule24': 'With many outs (12+) × 4 runs a little high.',
  'x.odds': 'The pot is 100 and your opponent bets 50: you pay 50 to win 200 (100 + 50 + 50), so you need 50 ÷ 200 = 25%.<br>Equity needed = call ÷ (pot after the bet + call).',
  'tip.odds': 'Smaller bets are cheaper to call — you need less equity.',
  'x.callfold': 'Call when your equity is above the equity the pot odds require; fold when it is below. That wins in the long run.',
  'tip.callfold': 'If you can win more later (implied odds) a call can be right even when a little short.',
  'x.ev': 'Expected value = equity × the pot you win − what you pay. A positive EV wins more the more often you make the play.',
  'tip.ev': 'Poker is about stacking +EV decisions, not about any single result.',
  'x.pre': 'Pairs, high cards (A, K), suited cards and connectors make strong starting hands. AA wins 85% against a random hand, 72o about 35%.',
  'tip.pre': 'Study → Starting hands shows all 169 hands.',
  'x.range': 'Six-handed guide: open-raise about the top 15% UTG, 27% from the cutoff and 45% on the button. The fewer players behind you, the wider you can play.',
  'tip.range': 'The blinds have money in already and defend a little wider.',
  'x.nuts': 'The best possible hand is the nuts. A paired board allows full houses, three of a suit allows flushes, connected ranks allow straights.',
  'tip.nuts': 'With the nuts you can bet big without fear.',
  'x.draws': 'Flush draw = four of a suit (9 outs). Open-ended = four in a row, either end completes (8). Gutshot = four with one gap (4).',
  'tip.draws': 'Draws are strong when they hit; when they miss they are usually just high card.',
  'x.omaha': 'In Omaha you must use exactly two of your four hole cards and exactly three board cards. Four hearts on the board with one heart in hand is NOT a flush.',
  'tip.omaha': 'There are 60 two-plus-three combinations — big hands are common, so think about the nuts.',
  'x.short': 'Short Deck removes the 2s–5s (36 cards). A flush beats a full house and three of a kind beats a straight (the ranking used here). A-6-7-8-9 is a straight.',
  'tip.short': 'Pairs and straights come more often and hands run closer together.',
  'x.stud': 'In Seven Card Stud you start with two down and one up. The lowest up card (equal ranks: ♣ < ♦ < ♥ < ♠) posts the bring-in. From 4th street the best showing hand acts first.',
  'tip.stud': 'You see every up card — remember which cards are dead.',
  'x.drawc': 'In Five Card Draw you change cards once. Guide: keep straights and better, draw one to two pair, two to trips, three to a pair, one to a four-flush or open-ended straight, else keep an ace and change the rest.',
  'tip.drawc': 'Everyone sees how many you draw; standing pat signals strength.',
  'q.rank': 'Which hand is stronger?', 'q.best7': 'The best hand of these seven cards?', 'q.outs': 'How many outs make a straight or flush (next card)?', 'q.r24f': '{n} outs on the flop. Your chance by the river is about…', 'q.r24t': '{n} outs on the turn. Your chance on the river is about…',
  'q.odds': 'The pot is {p} and the opponent bets {b}. The equity you need to call?', 'q.cf': 'Pot {p}, the bet {b}, your equity {e}. What do you do?', 'q.ev': 'The pot is {p} (bet included). You call {c} with {e} equity. Your EV?',
  'q.pre': 'Against one random hand, which has more equity?', 'q.range': 'Six-handed from {p}: do you open-raise {k}? (standard range)', 'q.nuts': 'Which holding makes the best hand on this board?', 'q.draw': 'What kind of draw is this?', 'q.omaha': 'Under Omaha rules this hand is…', 'q.short': 'Under Short Deck rules, which is stronger?', 'q.stud': 'Who posts the bring-in? (up cards)', 'q.drawc': 'How many cards do you draw?',
  'e.rank': 'A is {a}, B is {b}.', 'e.kicker': 'Same hand: compare the ranks that make it, then the kickers.', 'e.tie': 'Same hand and kickers: a split pot.', 'e.best7': 'The best five make {h}.', 'e.outs': '{n} cards complete it.',
  'e.r24': '{n} outs × {k} ≈ {r}% (exactly {x}%).', 'e.odds': 'Call {b} ÷ pot after the call {t} ≈ {r}%.', 'e.cf': 'Equity {e} vs {r} needed: {w}.', 'w.call': 'call', 'w.fold': 'fold',
  'e.ev': '{e} × {t} − {c} = {v}.', 'e.pre': '{a}: {ea}%, {b}: {eb}% (vs one random hand).', 'e.range': '{k} is a top-{n}% hand. The {p} range is the top {r}%.', 'e.nuts': 'The best holding makes {h}.',
  'dk.fd': 'Flush draw', 'dk.oe': 'Open-ended', 'dk.gs': 'Gutshot', 'dk.none': 'No draw', 'e.dk.fd': 'Four of a suit (9 outs).', 'e.dk.oe': 'Four in a row, either end makes a straight (8 outs).', 'e.dk.gs': 'Only the middle card makes the straight (4 outs).', 'e.dk.none': 'No single card makes a straight or flush.',
  'e.omaha': 'The best two-plus-three is {h}.', 'e.omaha2': '(With any five of nine it would be {w}, but not in Omaha.)', 'e.short': 'A is {a}, B is {b} — compared with the Short Deck ranking.', 'e.stud': 'The lowest up card pays (equal ranks: clubs lowest).', 'e.drawc': 'This is {h}: draw {n}.', dc: '{n}',
  'fq1': 'Nobody has bet. What can you NOT do?', 'fq1.a': 'Call', 'fq1.b': 'Check', 'fq1.c': 'Bet', 'fq1.e': 'With no bet there is nothing to call: check or bet.',
  'fq2': 'The player before you bet 20. What can you NOT do?', 'fq2.a': 'Check', 'fq2.b': 'Call', 'fq2.c': 'Fold', 'fq2.e': 'You cannot check once there is a bet.',
  'fq3': 'Everyone checked. What next?', 'fq3.a': 'The next card is dealt', 'fq3.b': 'The hand ends', 'fq3.c': 'The first player acts again', 'fq3.e': 'All bets are equal, so the next round starts.',
  'fq4': 'Everyone but you folded.', 'fq4.a': 'You win the pot without showing', 'fq4.b': 'You show your cards', 'fq4.c': 'The pot carries over', 'fq4.e': 'The last player left wins the pot.',
  'fq5': 'No limit, BB 2, the player before you raised to 6. The minimum raise is to…', 'fq5.a': '10', 'fq5.b': '8', 'fq5.c': '12', 'fq5.e': 'A raise must be at least the last raise (4): 6 + 4 = 10.',
  'fq6': 'Two hands are exactly equal at showdown.', 'fq6.a': 'They split the pot', 'fq6.b': 'The higher suit wins', 'fq6.c': 'The first bettor wins', 'fq6.e': 'Suits never rank in poker (only the stud bring-in uses them).',
  'pq1': 'The seat left of the button (D) is…', 'pq1.a': 'the small blind', 'pq1.b': 'the big blind', 'pq1.c': 'UTG', 'pq1.e': 'D → SB → BB.',
  'pq2': 'Who acts first preflop?', 'pq2.a': 'Left of the big blind (UTG)', 'pq2.b': 'The small blind', 'pq2.c': 'The button', 'pq2.e': 'The blinds act last preflop.',
